  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 221 PM CDT Sat Oct 3 2026\n\nInto the beginning of the upcoming work week, the forecast will \nremain dry, with a large area of high pressure over the Upper \nMidwest that will slowly depart the region, especially into Tuesday.\nOutside of an embedded shortwave passing over Winnipeg/Ontario,\nwith any rain chances staying well north of Iowa into midweek, \nquasi- zonal upper level flow is expected to persist, keeping \nconditions dry. The main story otherwise will be a gradual \nincrease in temperatures, with values into the low to mid 70s \nbecoming common Tue/Wed. The late work week will see an \nintensifying area of ridging over the western CONUS where a heat\ndome will dominate, which will put Iowa into a northwest flow \npattern aloft. This will likely introduce at least some \npotential for passing weak shortwave energy at times from the \nnorth, where long range guidance is starting to show by late \nThursday/early Friday, which could bring the first chance for a \nreturn of rain chances back into the state. Given low confidence\non specific track and evolution of features at this time \nthough, have left conditions dry, but this will be something to \nkeep a casual eye on in the coming days.",
